<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    HSK patch: gate VFE Mechanoids raids behind a minimum raid-points
    threshold so they don't appear in early-game / low-wealth / tribal
    scenarios.

    Why?
    Like the Junker pirates issue, low-tier VFE mechs (basic Lancer/Scyther
    variants) have low enough combatPower that the storyteller can squeeze
    them into a 200-400 point early raid budget. Result: tribal stone-age
    colonies getting hit by mech raids on day 4.

    Fix: every Combat pawnGroupMaker on VFE_Mechanoid gets
    <minTotalPoints>1500</minTotalPoints>. Below 1500 raid points
    (~80k+ wealth, mid-late game with charge tech researched) the
    storyteller can't pick a VFE Mechanoid combat group and falls back
    to vanilla mechs or other factions. At higher wealth they kick in
    normally.

    Settlement pawnGroupMakers are NOT gated — they govern base
    composition, not raid eligibility.

    Targets all 7 combat pawnGroupMakers (4 basic + 3 advanced) via
    kindDef="Combat" xpath selector.

    1500 is higher than the 800 threshold we use for Junker pirates
    because mechs are intended as a late-game threat — at 800 pts the
    storyteller could already fit a centipede or 5-6 lancers, which
    is brutal for a player without charge weapons or EMP. 1500 keeps
    mechs out until the player has the tech to fight back.
    Tune up if mechs still feel too early, down if they never appear.
-->
<Patch>

    <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/FactionDef[defName="VFE_Mechanoid"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"]</xpath>
        <value>
            <minTotalPoints>1500</minTotalPoints>
        </value>
    </Operation>

</Patch>
